※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 3014 LANG_SYNTAX_NOT_ASSOCIATIVE

※ '⊼' is not associative: (a ⊼ b) ⊼ c and a ⊼ (b ⊼ c) are different questions,
※ so writing three in a row is refused rather than given one of the two
※ meanings.  Parentheses say which was meant.
let a: bool = true
let b: bool = false
let c: bool = true

@[startup]
fn main() → bool:
    a ⊼ b ⊼ c
